-- debug-build-asserts-on-source-after-external-cmdsubst: a build with
-  `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug` (the only one where `assert()` is live)
-  aborts in `fd_setfd()` when a script sources a file whose path came
-  from a command substitution that ran an *external* command. A
-  substitution running only builtins (`$(echo ...)`) is fine, so the
-  fd left over from the forked child is what reaches `fd_setfd()`
-  without `FD_READ`/`FD_WRITE` set. Every `tests/*.sh` file starts
-  with exactly this pattern, so no test can run under a debug build.
+- debug-build-asserts-on-fd9-redirect-in-subshell-after-cmdsubst: a
+  build with `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug` (the only one where `assert()`
+  is live) aborts in `fd_setfd()` when a subshell opens an explicit
+  high-numbered fd (`exec 9>file`) after an earlier command
+  substitution has run. `redir_open()` -> `fdtable_openfd()` ->
+  `fdtable_track(..., FDTABLE_FORCE)` backfills every untracked fd
+  number between the shell's own bookkeeping and the newly-opened one
+  with synthetic placeholder structs (`fdtable_unexpected()`), and one
+  of those backfilled numbers turns out not to be a real, currently-
+  open fd (`fdtable_check()` returns 0), so the placeholder's `mode`
+  ends up empty. A different, narrower instance of this same "phantom
+  fd_list[] gap" class of bug (fd-subst-read-end-never-registered-in-
+  fd_list, `fixes/224`) is already fixed; this is a separate trigger
+  through explicit numbered-fd redirection rather than a substitution's
+  own bridging pipe, not yet root-caused.
 
   **Repro:**
   ```sh
   cmake -S . -B b -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug && cmake --build b -j
-  echo 'echo sourced' > /tmp/s.sh
-  printf 'D=$(dirname /tmp/x)\n. "$D/s.sh"\n' > /tmp/t.sh && ./b/shish /tmp/t.sh
+  cat <<'EOF' > /tmp/fd9.sh
+  TMPFILE=$(mktemp)
+  (exec 9>"$TMPFILE"
+  echo before >&9)
+  EOF
+  ./b/shish /tmp/fd9.sh
   # shish: src/fd/fd_setfd.c:13: fd_setfd: Assertion `d->mode & FD_READWRITE' failed.
   ```
 
